 "notes": [
  "Draft by an agent (#131), to be checked by eye: uv run python -m eval.redraw_overlay eval/redraw_bench/colorful-34.truth.json out.png --scale 6. Indices below are positions in each list, as the overlay labels them (w walls, o openings, r rooms, t texts).",
  "Uncertain entries carry \"uncertain\": true; texts and room names a person could not read for certain list the other readings in \"alternatives\" (reviewed 2026-11-16: the aula's vertical dimensions t2 and t6 could not be read for certain by the reviewer either). Any listed reading counts as right.",
  "Coordinates: x is the centre of source pixel x (as redraw_render.wall_mask fills it). Wall edges were measured from pixels at the half-way grey level, so a 2 px drawn line is 1-2 px wide here; the scan is turned about 1 degree, so long walls slope slightly.",
  "Walls drawn as two thin lines with a light fill between (attic knee walls, partitions) are one wall spanning both lines: w4, w9, w10, w11, w14, w15, w17, w19, w20, w21, w22, w25, w27, w40, w46-w49.",
  "Not walls: dimension lines (y 89-90 upper; x 159, x 195 upper; y 273, y 349, x 222 lower), dashed ceiling-slope and stair outlines, the spiral stair box, kitchen counters, sauna benches.",
  "w3, w13, w28: dark chimney masses, as polygons. w12 is the thick band between the two right-hand mh rooms; it continues as a stub into the upper aula to x 266.",
  "w4: the double line under the pale strip at the top left (y 61-66) is read as a wall closing the unnamed blue attic space above mh r0; it could be a beam or shelf line.",
  "w19, w20: double line with a diagonal between mh r0 and the spiral-stair space; could be a railing rather than a wall.",
  "w37: the kitchen's bottom band is taken across the red stair to the outer wall (x 33); over the stair it is drawn faintly under the red fill.",
  "o3: door at x 320, y 122-138, swinging into the upper aula, read from an arc centred on (320, 138); it could instead be a door in the wc top wall (w14) or the second leaf of o2.",
  "o4, o5: two arcs at the stair-hall corner (x 142-162, y 92-135). Read as a door in the top of the stair hall (hinge at x 162, swinging up into mh) and a door in w17 (hinge at y 115, swinging into the stair hall). May be one door drawn twice.",
  "o9: the box below the upper floor's bottom edge at x 184-226 is read as a window like the lower floor's; it may be the stair's lower flight instead.",
  "o13, o14: two arcs meeting at (117, 391) with an orange leaf line along x 118; read as a door in the kitchen's bottom wall and one in the pukuh top wall, both hinged at x 118 and swinging into the stair hall.",
  "o16: KPH | S door at x 152, y 430-447: leaf lines are seen but no clear arc; hinge and swing are a guess.",
  "o17, o18: the kuisti | aula door is read as a pair, a 22 px leaf hinged at x 210 and a 7 px leaf hinged at x 239, both swinging into the aula. The small one may be a frame detail.",
  "o19, o20: the entrance has two leaves on a frame box (x 243-277, y 455-466): inner on y 458 swinging into kuisti, outer on y 466 swinging outside (toward is below the house).",
  "Doors are drawn over continuous wall bands on this plan (no gap in the band), so each door's a-b lies on its wall's centre line.",
  "r5: upper wc name is written upside down (reads 'ɔm'); the circle below it is a toilet symbol.",
  "r7: written 'työh.' with a trailing dot; the umlaut is faint. redraw_score.fold keeps the dot, so a redraw reading 'työh' would not match.",
  "r11: handwriting reads 'Vaasto'; taken as 'varasto' (storage), the r merged into the a's. Could be scored as written instead.",
  "r13: 'KPH' written at about 60 degrees. r15: 'kuisti', the s looks like an r.",
  "Unnamed spaces, no room entry: top-left blue attic strip (x 28-168, y 11-61), spiral-stair space (x 29-141, y 136-197), stair hall left of the lower aula (x 82-168, y 367-406), small room right of kuisti (x 303-347, y 412-464, label h2169), closet in the kitchen (x 123-161, y 221-253), closet under the upper chimney (x 165-180, y 88-110).",
